      "QUESTION: How do I create a REST API with Python?\n",
      "CATEGORY: programming\n",
      "ANSWER: Creating a REST API in Python is a common task, and while you can use the built-in `http.server` module, the industry standard is to use a dedicated framework like **FastAPI** or **Flask**. FastAPI is currently preferred for new projects due to its speed, automatic documentation (Swagger/OpenAPI), and type hints.\n",
      "\n",
      "Below is a complete guide using **FastAPI**, as it provides the most modern and robust experience out of the box.\n",
      "\n",
      "### Prerequisites\n",
      "\n",
      "You will need Python 3.7 or higher installed on your machine.\n",
      "\n",
      "### Step 1: Install Dependencies\n",
      "\n",
      "First, install FastAPI and its dependency for serving static files (like HTML for Swagger UI):\n",
      "\n",
      "```bash\n",
      "pip install fastapi uvicorn\n",
      "```\n",
      "\n",
      "*   `fastapi`: The web framework.\n",
      "*   `uvicorn`: The ASGI server used to run the application.\n",
      "\n",
      "### Step 2: Create the Application Code\n",
      "\n",
      "Create a file named `main.py`. This code defines a simple REST API with endpoints for creating, reading, updating, and deleting (CRUD) operations on a list of users.\n",
      "\n",
      "```python\n",
      "from fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, Depends\n",
      "from pydantic import BaseModel\n",
      "from typing import List, Optional\n",
      "from datetime import datetime\n",
      "\n",
      "# Initialize the FastAPI application\n",
      "app = FastAPI(title=\"Python REST API Example\", version=\"1.0\")\n",
      "\n",
      "# --- Data Models (Pydantic) ---\n",
      "class User(BaseModel):\n",
      "    id: int\n",
      "    name: str\n",
      "    email: str\n",
      "\n",
      "# In-memory storage for demonstration purposes\n",
      "users_db: List[User] = []\n",
      "user_counter = 1\n",
      "\n",
      "# --- Helper Functions ---\n",
      "def get_user_by_id(user_id: int) -> Optional[User]:\n",
      "    for user in users_db:\n",
      "        if user.id == user_id:\n",
      "            return user\n",
      "    return None\n",
      "\n",
      "# --- API Endpoints ---\n",
      "\n",
      "@app.get(\"/\")\n",
      "async def root():\n",
      "    \"\"\"Root endpoint returning API info\"\"\"\n",
      "    return {\"message\": \"Welcome to the Python REST API\", \"docs\": \"/docs\"}\n",
      "\n",
      "@app.post(\"/users/\", response_model=User)\n",
      "async def create_user(user_data: User):\n",
      "    \"\"\"Create a new user\"\"\"\n",
      "    global user_counter\n",
      "    \n",
      "    # Check if ID already exists (optional validation)\n",
      "    existing = get_user_by_id(user_data.id)\n",
      "    if existing:\n",
      "        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"User ID already exists\")\n",
      "\n",
      "    # Create new user object\n",
      "    new_user = User(id=user_counter, name=user_data.name, email=user_data.email)\n",
      "    users_db.append(new_user)\n",
      "    user_counter += 1\n",
      "    \n",
      "    return new_user\n",
      "\n",
      "@app.get(\"/users/\")\n",
      "async def list_users():\n",
      "    \"\"\"List all users\"\"\"\n",
      "    return {\"users\": users_db}\n",
      "\n",
      "@app.get(\"/users/{user_id}\")\n",
      "async def get_user(user_id: int):\n",
      "    \"\"\"Get a specific user by ID\"\"\"\n",
      "    user = get_user_by_id(user_id)\n",
      "    \n",
      "    if not user:\n",
      "        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"User not found\")\n",
      "    \n",
      "    return user\n",
      "\n",
      "@app.put(\"/users/{user_id}\")\n",
      "async def update_user(user_id: int, user_data: User):\n",
      "    \"\"\"Update an existing user\"\"\"\n",
      "    user = get_user_by_id(user_id)\n",
      "    \n",
      "    if not user:\n",
      "        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"User not found\")\n",
      "\n",
      "    # Update fields (excluding ID to prevent accidental changes)\n",
      "    user.name = user_data.name\n",
      "    user.email = user_data.email\n",
      "    \n",
      "    return user\n",
      "\n",
      "@app.delete(\"/users/{user_id}\")\n",
      "async def delete_user(user_id: int):\n",
      "    \"\"\"Delete a user\"\"\"\n",
      "    global users_db\n",
      "    \n",
      "    initial_len = len(users_db)\n",
      "    users_db = [u for u in users_db if u.id != user_id]\n",
      "    \n",
      "    if len(users_db) == initial_len:\n",
      "        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"User not found\")\n",
      "    \n",
      "    return {\"message\": f\"User {user_id} deleted successfully\"}\n",
      "\n",
      "# --- Run the Server ---\n",
      "if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n",
      "    import uvicorn\n",
      "    # Run on port 8000 by default\n",
      "    uvicorn.run(app, host=\"0.0.0.0\", port=8000)\n",
      "```\n",
      "\n",
      "### Step 3: How to Run the API\n",
      "\n",
      "1.  Save the code above as `main.py`.\n",
      "2.  Open your terminal in the directory containing the file.\n",
